vampire sasha ivliskova~
&+Mthe vampire of &+LS&+Ma&+Ls&+Mh&+La &+MI&+Lv&+Ml&+Li&+Ms&+Lk&+Mo&+Lv&+Ma~
&+MBetrayed by her love, the vampire of &+LS&+Ma&+Ls&+Mh&+La &+MI&+Lv&+Ml&+Li&+Ms&+Lk&+Mo&+Lv&+Ma screams in torment.
~
   &+MFor many years, Sasha Ivliskova served as the Burgomaster of Barovia
&+Mand was deeply beloved by her folk. Beautiful and noble, Sasha Ivliskova
&+Moriginally sought out Strahd to petition for an end to the darkness that
&+Mplagued her homeland, but instead became the first to live the same night
&+M-mare that many women would follow.
   &+MAfter the Burgomaster's expedition to Castle Ravenloft, there was a
&+Mperiod of stillness and calm in the great realm of Barovia that would
&+Mnever repeat. The mists subsided, the wolf presence thinned greatly,
&+Mand the undead attacks all but ceased. Days turned into weeks and rumors
&+Mfloated that Sasha Ivliskova had stormed the castle and killed Strahd
&+Mpersonally. Others spoke of a second coming of Strahd's love, and source
&+Mof his anguish, Tatyana, reincarnated through Sasha Ivliskova.
   &+MAfter having turned her into a vampire, Strahd no longer saw Sasha as
&+MTatyana and his interest in her quickly evaporated. She was cast-off into
&+Man eternal slumber, much like his own, in the Catacombs of Ravenloft.
~
