&-w&+RPidlwick II&N~
&-w&+RPidlwick II, the wind-up mechanical jester, skips through here happily.
~
   &+WPidlwick was a fool of the visiting Duchess of Dorfniya Dilsnya, a royal
&+Wof local nobility who frequented Castle Ravenloft during the reign of Barov
&+Wand Ravenovia Von Zarovich. After several visits of constant entertainment
&+Wfor Sergei and his wife-to-be, Tatyana, the Duchess commissioned the great
&+Wtoymaker Fritz Von Weerg to craft a clockwork toy duplicate - Pidlwick II.
   &+rDuring a cold winter, Duchess Dorfinya had grown ill, stranded in the
&+rCastle with Pidlwick and his double. Unfortunately, she gave-in to her
&+rillness and died. Pidlwick II couldn't move or jest quite like his human
&+r&+rcounterpart, and only made his hosts cringe. After falling into disuse,
&+rPidwlick II grew jealous, knowing that it could never get the attention
&+rit wanted so long as its predecessor lived, and murdered its human counter-
&+rpart by pushing him down a long flight of stairs. Pidlwick II attempted to
&+rpick up where the first left off, but it failed miserably, even disturbing
&+rTatyana before getting locked away in a closet for years to come.
   &+LAfter Sergei and Tatyana's demise and the castle becoming largely empty
&+Lof the living, Pidwlick II emerged and began stalking through the corridors.
&+LEven Strahd knew of its murderous tendencies and took advantage of it from
&+Ltime to time - finally prompting a smile by a Von Zarovich.
~
